WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.260
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.000
I’m back!

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.590
I’m back, Wanpachi.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.500
Go on, Eevee, you come out too.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.510
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.940
It’ll be a little while
until I’m finished with my work.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:38.760
Okay!

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.520
I’ll go and read a book
in your room, Dad.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.340
Sure.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.770
What should I choose...?

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.520
Huh? Why...?

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.530
That’s beautiful!

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.280
“The Tale of the
Luminous Maze Forest and You”?

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.070
Dad, do you have a moment?

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:06.290
What is it?

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:10.130
Can you tell me about
these Pokémon here?

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:14.290
Oh, that’s the Galarian Ponyta
and Gallop.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.710
Huh? They’re nothing like
the ones I’ve seen.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:21.200
In the Kanto region...
they look like this, right?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.930
Huh?
So they’re different in Galar?!

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.140
Ponyta! Galarian Form!
One-Horned Pokémon! Psychic type!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.540
Its small horn hides a healing power!

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.430
With its Heal Pulse,
any slight wound you have will be healed!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:44.730
Gallop! Galarian Form! One-Horned Pokémon!
Fairy/Psychic type!

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.650
The evolved form of Ponyta!

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.990
Brave and prideful!

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.960
This Pokémon dashes airily through the forest, its steps aided
by the psychic power stored in the fur on its fetlocks!

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.660
Ponyta and Gallop...

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:01.350
It’s rare to see you asking
about a Pokémon, Koharu.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.200
I guess I was just curious.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.690
I... I’d like to see them.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.050
Me, too.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.760
See and then catch them!

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.850
Then you should all
go and see them together.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.170
All right!

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.020
Thank you, Dad!

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:17.770
And so, Satoshi, Go,
and even Koharu,

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:19.660
Luminous Maze Forest, Galar Region
And so, Satoshi, Go,
and even Koharu,

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:25.070
have arrived at the
Luminous Maze Forest in Galar.
Luminous Maze Forest, Galar Region

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.610
Luminous Maze Forest, Galar Region

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.310
It’s like it’s already night!

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.680
You could do a
test of courage here!

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.080
Hurry up, let’s go.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.420
Oh, it got brighter!

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.250
Wow.
What a strange forest!

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:49.470
Yeah!
It’s all just like the book said!

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.530
According to Dad,

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:58.150
Galarian Ponyta and Gallop live hidden deep in the forest,
and almost never show themselves!

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:07.160
Apparently, they took on a special form after
absorbing this forest’s mysterious energy over generations.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.480
That sounds really exciting!

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:13.420
If they almost never show themselves,
that just makes me want ‘em even <i>more!</i>

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.300
Okay! Let’s get going!

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.540
Yeah!

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.270
Nemush! Illuminating Pokémon!
Grass/Fairy type!

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:29.970
They scatter flickering spores
that put enemies to sleep!

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.860
Wait, Nemush!
Nemush, wait!

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.320
What is it?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.380
A Ponyta!

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.090
Hold on, Eevee!

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.090
Aceburn!

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.350
Monster Ball, go!

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.910
Nemush’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.420
All right!

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.150
Good work, Go.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.740
Huh? Where’d...

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.710
...Koharu and Eevee go?

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:55.510
Eevee!

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.230
No way...

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.880
Easy does it...

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.680
Ponyta!

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.010
Gallop?!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.550
You’re hurt...

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.900
It’s just like I saw before...

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.920
Are you okay?

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:41.910
You want me to help Gallop?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.570
Is that... Heal Pulse?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:01.450
It’s hurt badly enough that
even Ponyta can’t heal it...

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.980
Did it slip and fall down
into the ravine?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.550
I know!

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:18.740
There was a part in this book
where a Gallop was being healed.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:22.130
Dew from the rainbow flowers
blooming deep in the forest...

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.620
...has a healing energy,
and drinking it makes you better, it says!

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.570
Look!

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:31.090
I’ll go and get it!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.820
Ponyta?

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:39.050
You’ll guide me there?

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:42.580
Hold on.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.120
I’ll be back soon!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.420
Calling! Calling! Calling! Calling!

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.410
Hey! Koharu!
Calling! Calling! Calling! Calling!

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.620
Calling! Calling! Calling! Calling!

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.240
It’s not connecting...
Calling! Calling! Calling! Calling!

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:01.750
Calling! Calling! Calling! Calling!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:02.810
Huh...
Calling! Calling! Calling! Calling!

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:07.200
Well, she has Eevee,
so she should be okay.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:11.610
Even when we used to do tests of courage when camping,
she’d never get scared.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.740
Really?

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.410
She’s got more guts
than you’d expect.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:18.460
So as long as we find her before it gets dark,
she should be fine.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.910
Though, I guess it’s dark already...

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.110
It started raining.

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:28.430
It’s just a shower.
It won’t last, yeah?

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.220
Go. Look at that.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.990
Doesn’t it look brighter over there?

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.390
Never expected to find a town
deep in this forest.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:47.050
Yeah. Hopefully Koharu’s here too.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.150
Excuse me, you two.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.650
You lack pink.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.340
Sorry.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.680
Hello.

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:59.730
We’re looking for a friend of ours.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:03.390
Did you see a girl
with an Eevee anywhere?

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:07.350
If you answer my quiz correctly,
I’ll tell you!

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.100
Question!
What is my favorite color?

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.230
1: Pink.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.400
2: Purple.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:17.930
Go, what do you think?

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.110
She said “You lack pink,”
didn’t she?

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.310
That means...

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:23.970
1! Pink!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:27.690
Bzzzt!
The answer was 2, purple.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:31.220
Pink is what I like to see in other people,
but it’s not what I like for myself.

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.040
Okay, next question.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.190
There’s more questions?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.420
Question! How old am I?

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.050
1: 16 years old.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:43.550
2: 88 years old!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:48.210
2! 88 years old!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.590
Bzzzt!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:55.980
Well, you’re not wrong.
But you could’ve been a little more sensitive.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.520
You two, you lack pink
in your hearts!

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:01.430
S-Sorry...

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.430
Let me give you some.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.770
Here! Wear this.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.340
I can’t get through.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.990
Go and Satoshi
must be worried about me.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.510
The rain stopped!

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.460
Yeah. Let’s go!

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.830
Are you okay, Eevee?

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.780
Okay, I’ve got to get going, too!

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.550
Should we take a little break?

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.420
You want a drink too, Ponyta?

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.850
Heal Pulse...

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.360
Wow!

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.510
Thank you, Ponyta!

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:01.350
It’s healed! Wow!

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:02.880
You used Heal Pulse on me?

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.090
Thank you, Eevee!

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:27.070
Over there! The rainbow flowers!

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.730
We’re nearly there. Let’s hurry!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.000
W-What?

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.480
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:56.140
Beroba. Mean Pokémon.
Evil/Fairy type.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:00.500
Through its nose, it sucks in the emanations
produced by people and Pokémon when they feel annoyed.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.520
It thrives off this negative energy.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.830
What?! “Mean Pokémon”?

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.170
Those are mine!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.730
Eevee!

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.300
Hey!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.880
Give them back!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.350
Hey, listen.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.330
Could you please let us through?

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:42.120
We really need dew from
those flowers over there.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.130
What should I do...?

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.150
I don’t have time for this...

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:06.960
Eevee?

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.350
Looks like they’re all having fun...

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:02.020
Maybe the Beroba just
wanted us to play with them?

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:08.200
Now you’ve done it!
Follow me, Ponyta!

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:44.030
Playing along with their mischief
was really tiring...

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:19.270
Thank you, Beroba!

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:34.660
Now, let’s hurry back to Gallop.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.970
Gallop, drink this.

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:16.360
Can you stand up?

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.160
But why?
Your wound’s healed.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:26.600
Are you low on stamina?

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:44.970
Ponyta, Eevee, go for it!

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.320
Make Gallop better!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.280
Gallop!

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.160
That’s great!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.690
It’s so beautiful!

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.950
Okay, next question.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:43.140
How much longer is this quiz?

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.950
Sorry about this, Pikachu...

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.080
You too, Aceburn...

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:52.580
This is the last question.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.790
Who do you think that is,
over there?

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.070
Koharu! Eevee!

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:01.930
And a Galarian Ponyta and Gallop!

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:07.310
I trusted the correct answer was to wait here,
rather than move blindly.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.810
And she must be a fine lass.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:15.980
The cautious Ponyta and Gallop
don’t let just anyone ride them.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:18.100
Thank you for helping me get here.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.690
You’re awesome, Koharu!

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.690
Wait...

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:24.610
They left...

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:27.620
You <i>had</i> to raise your voice...

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.270
I’m glad you’re both safe,
Go and Satoshi.

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:33.930
Koharu!
How’d it feel to ride on Gallop?

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:35.560
Great, right?

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:36.500
Y-Yeah...

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.090
I knew it!

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.510
Must’ve been great
to befriend them, Koharu...

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:42.760
Yeah!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.630
I hope I see them again!

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:04.290
Huh? What was I...

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.510
Oh, I fell asleep.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.400
Hey, Koharu!

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:13.360
Come in!

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:15.430
The Director says he’s done with his work!

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.000
Oh, right.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.340
Thank you.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:37.470
Koharu and Eevee have met new Pokémon
and shared new experiences.

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:42.980
They’ll surely never forget the dreamlike
time they spent in the forest.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:51.730
Mew!

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:52.480
Warrgle!

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:53.270
Runpappa!

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.040
Pawou!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:54.780
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:55.570
Strike!

00:21:55.570 --> 00:21:56.370
Cresselia!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:57.080
Amakaji!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.890
Jirachi!

00:21:57.890 --> 00:21:58.690
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.690 --> 00:21:59.460
Kibago!

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.230
Gonbe!

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.010
Bayleaf!

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:02.510
Freezer!

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:03.700
Zacian!

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:20.550
Mew!

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:21.380
Wooper!

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:22.100
Pachirisu!

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:22.950
Sunaba!

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:23.610
Absol!

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:24.470
Lunala!

00:22:24.470 --> 00:22:25.280
Rabbifoot!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.060
Tropius!

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:26.830
Sunahebi!

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:27.700
Vibrava!

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:28.350
Burshamo!

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:29.120
Mokuroh!

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:29.940
Rotom!

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:30.660
Mooland!

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:31.440
Dodorio!

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:32.160
Otosupus!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:32.980
Swanna!

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:33.730
Nazonokusa!

00:22:33.730 --> 00:22:34.550
Samehada!

00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:35.320
Darkrai!

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:36.000
Iwanko!

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:36.830
Cortoise!

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:37.660
Scorupi!

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:38.440
Pippi!

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:39.160
Pinpuku!

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:39.940
Kunugidama!

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:40.680
Mankey!

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:41.490
Kimori!

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:42.310
Ligray!

00:22:42.310 --> 00:22:43.740
Rayquaza!

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:44.470
Zamazenta!

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.580
Now, onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.860
Go!

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:13.520
The Castle of Chivalry?

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:16.120
Apparently they train Pokémon
and their trainers!

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:21.630
I welcome you here!
I am Gampi of the Kalos Elite Four, the Man of Steel!

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:23.800
Th-The Man of Steel?!

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:25.800
He’s really intense!

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.050
Okay, Kamonegi!
Let’s challenge the Elite Four!

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.890
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:33.910
Gampi of the Elite Four!
The Castle of Chivalry!!
